# Google Places API key — discovery uses the official Places API only.
# Never scrape Google Search/Maps. Copy this file to .env and fill in.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# Deprecated: GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY was the old name for the same key. It is
# still read, with a warning, for one release. Rename it and delete this note.
#
# The name matters beyond tidiness: this key is for the Places API and nothing
# else, and a variable called GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY invites the next person to
# reach for Maps — which is the surface CLAUDE.md forbids touching.

# Google Safe Browsing v4 key, for scripts/domain-safety/check.mjs — the
# pre-purchase check that says whether a domain is carrying somebody else's
# reputation. Free, and separate from the Places key on purpose: two keys with
# two API restrictions means a leak of one is not a leak of both.
#
# Unset, the Safe Browsing half reports "unavailable" and the Wayback half
# still runs. It never degrades into a green tick it did not earn.
#
# The request shape and every response path are testable without a key at all:
#   node scripts/domain-safety/stub-server.mjs --mode flagged
#   node scripts/domain-safety/check.mjs <domain> --stub-safe-browsing <url>
SAFE_BROWSING_API_KEY=
